DateLyrics uses Brad Conte's public-domain DES implementation:
https://github.com/B-Con/crypto-algorithms

The upstream author releases this code into the public domain without restrictions
or warranties. DateLyrics namespaces its symbols, uses unsigned shifts, and applies
QQ's legacy encoding differences: S-box 2 entry 23 is 15, S-box 4 entry 53 is 10,
the PC-2 right-half offset is 27, and bytes are reversed within each 32-bit input
and output word. This decoder only reads lyric data; it does not secure credentials.
